<title>FRANCE: MOTOR RACING-LE MANS 24-HOURS PLACINGS AFTER THREE HOURS.</title>
<headline>MOTOR RACING-LE MANS 24-HOURS PLACINGS AFTER THREE HOURS.</headline>
<dateline>LE MANS, France 1997-06-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading placings after</p>
<p>three hours of the Le Mans 24 Hours race on Saturday:</p>
<p>1. Yannick Dalmas (France)/Ralf Kelleners (Germany)/Emmanuel</p>
<p>Collard (France) Porsche 911 GT1 45 laps</p>
<p>2. Hans Stuck (Germany)/Bob Wollek (France)/Thierry Boutsen</p>
<p>(Belgium) Porsche 911 GT1 17.848 seconds behind</p>
<p>3. Michele Alboreto (Italy)/Stefan Johansson (Sweden)/Tom</p>
<p>Kristensen (Denmark) TWR Porsche-Joest 44.587 seconds</p>
<p>4. Jean-Marc Gounon (France)/Pierre-Henri Raphanel (France)</p>
<p>/Anders Olofsson (Sweden) McLaren BMW F1GTR 2 minutes 04.509</p>
<p>5. Eric van de Poele (Belgium)/Riccardo Patrese (Italy)/Aguri</p>
<p>Suzuki (Japan) Nissan R390 one lap behind</p>
<p>6. Andrew Scott (Britain)/Ray Bellm (Britain)/Masanori Sekiya</p>
<p>(Japan) McLaren BMW F1GTR</p>
<p>7. Peter Kox (Netherlands)/Roberto Ravaglia (Italy)/Eric Helary</p>
<p>(France) McLaren BMW F1GTR</p>
<p>8. Christophe Bouchut (France)/Andy Evans (U.S.)/Bertrand</p>
<p>Gachot (France) Porsche 911 GT1</p>
<p>9. Kazuyoshi Hoshino (Japan)/Erik Comas (France)/Masahiko</p>
<p>Kageyama (Japan) Nissan R390</p>
<p>10. Didier Cottaz (France)/Jerome Policand (France)/Marc</p>
<p>Goosens (Belgium) Courage C41 all one lap</p>
</text>
